  "solutions": [
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_157"
      ],
      "explanation": "Since \\(x=a/b\\), divide both the numerator and denominator by \\(b\\) to make that ratio appear. This is valid because \\(b\\ne0\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{a+b}{a-b}\n=\\frac{a/b+1}{a/b-1}\n=\\frac{x+1}{x-1}.\n\\]\nMoreover, \\(x-1=(a-b)/b\\ne0\\), so the resulting fraction is defined under the original assumptions. The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{x+1}{x-1}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
      "id": "divide-by-b",
      "sourceRef": "amc/1991_AMC_12_Q07#divide-by-b",
      "title": "Reveal the given ratio"
    }
  ],
